<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Hayrick Butte Loop</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:249-5: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.406476" lon="-121.868868"><ele>1441.8</ele><name>Hoodoo Sno-Park (south lot)</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:hoodoo-sno-park (OSM way 159251390); confidence: high; pdf_page: 252; quote: park as far south as possible in Hoodoo Sno-Park, then on skis aim for the low pass to the south between the two buttes</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.403500" lon="-121.873500"><ele>1473.0</ele><name>Valley between the buttes</name><desc>source: DEM valley floor (4,870 ft) between Hoodoo Butte and Hayrick Butte; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 252; quote: Spectacular cliffs to the east dominate the narrow valley leading to the pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.400600" lon="-121.876800"><ele>1518.1</ele><name>Pass between Hoodoo and Hayrick buttes</name><desc>source: north end of OSM Forest Road 2690-864 (way 366749107); DEM saddle about 5,050 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 252; book_elev_ft: 5000; quote: At the pass, enjoy a view of Big Lake and Mount Washington to the south</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.391800" lon="-121.876400"><ele>1458.2</ele><name>Foot of the slope west of Hayrick</name><desc>source: south end of OSM Forest Road 2690-864; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 252; quote: follow along the pass's contour and descend moderate slopes to the open flats of the Airstrip Burn</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.391000" lon="-121.866000"><ele>1446.4</ele><name>Airstrip Burn below Hayrick's south side</name><desc>source: placed on the flats south of Hayrick Butte (DEM 4,740 ft); confidence: low; pdf_page: 252; quote: then turn east to join the South Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.392500" lon="-121.861500"><ele>1437.8</ele><name>Hayrick SE corner</name><desc>source: placed off the butte's south-east foot (DEM about 4,720 ft); confidence: low; pdf_page: 252; quote: It is possible to ski to your car by staying close to the base of Hayrick Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.396500" lon="-121.861500"><ele>1448.8</ele><name>Under the east cliffs (south)</name><desc>source: placed on the flat just east of the cliff foot (DEM about 4,750-4,800 ft); the 1994 South Loop west leg 'directly under the cliffs of Hayrick Butte' (pdf 251); confidence: low; pdf_page: 252; quote: It is possible to ski to your car by staying close to the base of Hayrick Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.400500" lon="-121.862500"><ele>1459.9</ele><name>Under the east cliffs (north)</name><desc>source: placed east of the cliff foot (DEM about 4,770 ft); confidence: low; pdf_page: 252; quote: It is possible to ski to your car by staying close to the base of Hayrick Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.403500" lon="-121.865000"><ele>1458.4</ele><name>Hayrick NE foot</name><desc>source: placed below the north-east nose (DEM about 4,790 ft); confidence: low; pdf_page: 252; quote: It is possible to ski to your car by staying close to the base of Hayrick Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.406476" lon="-121.868868"><ele>1441.8</ele><name>Hoodoo Sno-Park (south lot)</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:hoodoo-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 252; quote: It is possible to ski to your car by staying close to the base of Hayrick Butte</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Hayrick Butte Loop</name><desc>1. Hoodoo Sno-Park (south lot) -&gt; Valley between the buttes: straight (medium), 0.31 mi | 2. Valley between the buttes -&gt; Pass between Hoodoo and Hayrick buttes: straight (medium), 0.26 mi | 3. Pass between Hoodoo and Hayrick buttes -&gt; Foot of the slope west of Hayrick: osm (medium), 0.81 mi | 4. Foot of the slope west of Hayrick -&gt; Airstrip Burn below Hayrick's south side: straight (low), 0.52 mi | 5. Airstrip Burn below Hayrick's south side -&gt; Hayrick SE corner: straight (low), 0.25 mi | 6. Hayrick SE corner -&gt; Under the east cliffs (south): straight (low), 0.28 mi | 7. Under the east cliffs (south) -&gt; Under the east cliffs (north): straight (low), 0.28 mi | 8. Under the east cliffs (north) -&gt; Hayrick NE foot: straight (low), 0.24 mi | 9. Hayrick NE foot -&gt; Hoodoo Sno-Park (south lot): straight (medium), 0.28 mi</desc>
